WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.049 --> 00:00:01.049
Speaker 1: All right.

00:00:01.049 --> 00:00:03.550
A couple of media stories that I want to discuss
with you.

00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:08.130
There is a very interesting realignment happening
in the wake of Tucker Carlson's firing from

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:10.450
Fox News and, of course, the Dominion.

00:00:10.450 --> 00:00:17.080
Nearly $800 million settlement obtained from
Fox, as well as the firing on CNN of CEO Chris

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:22.439
Licht after only a year, which included a
number of very strange programing decisions.

00:00:22.439 --> 00:00:30.019
Newsweek is now reporting MSNBC dethroned
Fox News after years long ratings dominance.

00:00:30.019 --> 00:00:37.340
Fox News his yearslong streak of rating dominance
has ended, with new data showing it ceding

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:41.200
the top spot to its rival network, MSNBC.

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:44.911
Nielsen data regarding the week ending this
past Sunday was shared on Twitter by A.J.

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:48.460
Katz, a reporter specializing in the cable
news business.

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:55.120
According to the data, Fox's primetime 8 to
11 p.m. Eastern viewership averaged 1.504

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:56.379
million.

00:00:56.379 --> 00:01:02.300
The average viewership for the more left leaning
MSNBC over the same time frame averaged 1.52

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:03.590
million.

00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:08.840
Narrowly beating out the conservative network
that has long been a leader in cable news

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:10.270
viewership.

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:12.750
There are a lot of important things to discuss
here.

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:17.750
First and foremost, this is a very small margin
of victory for MSNBC.

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:23.229
And I do want to remind everybody that I couch
this story not as I'm cheering about MSNBC.

00:01:23.229 --> 00:01:29.650
MSNBC is a corporate media outlet, just like
all the others that has chosen a center left

00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:33.640
very establishment Democratic Party editorial
position.

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:36.600
It's well to my right, it's not super exciting.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:42.090
There's a media story here, and I want people
to understand that it's a media story totally

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:45.840
separate from my particular political views.

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:52.409
MSNBC is being helped significantly right
now by, number one, the fiasco and disaster

00:01:52.409 --> 00:02:00.549
at Fox News, in which Fox was exposed in court
for lying to their audience in order to get

00:02:00.549 --> 00:02:06.180
ratings on the basis of playing coy and in
many cases overtly supporting Donald Trump's

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:08.590
false claims that he won the 2020 election.

00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:12.780
To further conservative talking points to
maintain access to Republicans in power by

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:18.270
repeating or allowing them to repeat uncritically
their talking points, that has been really

00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:22.470
bad for Fox News, the firing of Tucker, etc.

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:24.560
We then have CNN.

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:32.319
CNN with a disastrous year with now fired
former CEO Chris Licht at the helm.

00:02:32.319 --> 00:02:41.230
And so MSNBC truly has benefited from problems
suffered by Fox News and by CNN.

00:02:41.230 --> 00:02:48.540
What this actually means for the future of
24 hour news media remains an open question,

00:02:48.540 --> 00:02:51.019
with fragmentation of the audience.

00:02:51.019 --> 00:02:55.720
Thanks to streaming and to some degree, independent
media like our show and so many others that

00:02:55.720 --> 00:03:03.890
are available asynchronously online in podcasts,
YouTube, tik-tok, etc. form with a desire

00:03:03.890 --> 00:03:11.200
from audiences for a different type of presentation
that maybe feels a little less corporate and

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:14.020
a little more intimate in some way.

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:21.000
This little blip in which Fox is down and
MSNBC is up may remain or it may not as far

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.440
as cable news ratings are concerned.

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:29.610
But my prediction is that other forms of news
media and political analysis are going to

00:03:29.610 --> 00:03:32.790
continue growing as a share of the total news
media audience.

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:34.850
Now, you might say, well, David, you would
like that, right?

00:03:34.850 --> 00:03:36.480
Because you benefit from that.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:37.489
We're doing fine already.

00:03:37.489 --> 00:03:39.189
We don't need to grow anymore.

00:03:39.189 --> 00:03:40.189
Everything's fine.

00:03:40.189 --> 00:03:45.099
It's and I'm not even saying the David Pacman
show is what's going to grow necessarily.

00:03:45.099 --> 00:03:49.640
It's a question about the direction of people's
tastes and appetites.

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:54.560
And there's a real question mark now, the
next 18 months or how many months do we have?

00:03:54.560 --> 00:04:00.599
Five and 12, 17 months, the next 17 months,
not even 16 and a half months leading up to

00:04:00.599 --> 00:04:08.329
the 2024 election are going to be extraordinarily
important in seeing what niches different

00:04:08.329 --> 00:04:10.250
media outlets choose.

00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:12.860
We don't know what Fox is going to do from
here on out.

00:04:12.860 --> 00:05:36.520
We also don't know what MSNBC is going to
do, but very interesting nonetheless.

